  "reason": "RNA-only PCA single-profile is much stronger than image-only ResNet single-profile in both accuracy and F1, making RNA the current promising direction while still leaving uncertainty about whether multiprofile aggregation can improve it. config_002 keeps the same PCA RNA encoder and model setting as the best completed experiment and changes only to multiprofile with simple avgpool, directly testing the profile/aggregation effect. It is the best next experiment under a limited budget because it exploits the strongest baseline with the simplest multiprofile variant, and it will either yield a stronger RNA baseline or clarify that profile aggregation is not helping before adding more complex encoders, image modalities, or fusion."
